SUMMARY:Graduate Events: Donovan Rasamoelison\, University of California\
 , Santa Barbara - “More Paperwork\, Less Fraud? The Welfare Impact of 
 Compliance Documentation Beyond Screening”
LOCATION:North Hall 2111
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Donovan Rasamoelison\, University of California\, Sa
 nta Barbara\nTitle: “More Paperwork\, Less Fraud? The Welfare Impact o
 f Compliance Documentation Beyond Screening”\n\nThis paper investigate
 s whether compliance documentation offers incremental fraud deterrence i
 n the presence of initial ex-ante screening by leveraging a policy featu
 re of the Paycheck Protection Program - a loan-size threshold that waive
 d compliance documentation requirements for loan forgiveness. On the one
  hand\, the waiver may encourage firms with true loan eligibility below 
 the threshold to opportunistically inflate their loan requests up to the
  threshold. On the other hand\, firms with true loan amounts above the t
 hreshold may strategically reduce their loans to avoid the administrativ
 e burden of compliance. Quantitatively\, opportunistic overclaiming was 
 limited and the loan-reducing effect outweighed the loan-increasing effe
 ct\, resulting in a net welfare gain of $0.03 per dollar borrowed from t
 he documentation waiver. These results indicate that compliance document
 ation requirements impose substantial burden while providing limited mar
 ginal fraud deterrence in the presence of initial screening.\n\nhttps://
 econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2026/practice-job-talk-donovan-rasamoelison-uni
 versity-california-santa-barbara
URL:https://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2026/practice-job-talk-donovan-rasam
 oelison-university-california-santa-barbara
CATEGORIES:GRADUATE
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
